---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "@/components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";
import { SITE } from "@/config";
---

<Layout title={`About · ${SITE.title}`}>
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content" class="app-layout pt-10 pb-20">
    <article class="max-w-prose-app">
      <header class="mb-12">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-muted-foreground">
          About
        </p>
        <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-5">
          <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
            <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
              NihilDigit
            </h1>
            <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-sm text-muted-foreground">Shibo Liu</p>
          </div>
          <a
            href="/Shibo_Liu_CV.pdf"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="cv-peek group ml-auto inline-block shrink-0 self-start"
          >
            <span class="cv-peek__frame">
              <span class="cv-peek__paper">
                <span class="cv-peek__fold" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="cv-peek__label" aria-hidden="true">CV.pdf</span>
                <span class="cv-peek__title">View CV</span>
                <span class="sr-only">, PDF opens in a new tab</span>
                <span class="cv-peek__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="cv-peek__rule cv-peek__rule--short" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </span>
            </span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section class="space-y-6 text-foreground leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          I'm a third-year undergraduate at
          <a
            href="https://www.ncst.edu.cn/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent"
          >North China University of Science and Technology</a>, studying
          intelligence science.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/NihilDigit/RAFNet"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent"
          >RAFNet</a> was my first academic project, and also where I
          learned computer vision by doing it. We built a classifier for
          student behavior in crowded classrooms on top of
          <a
            href="https://github.com/boycehbz/GroupRec"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent"
          >GroupRec</a>, an existing hypergraph encoder, with a gated fusion
          head; I ran the experiments. It's under review at The Visual
          Computer.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a
            href="/tongxing"
            class="underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent"
          >TongXing</a> ran in parallel with that work, but from the
          deployment side. It won a provincial second prize in 4C2026 and
          is now in the national round. The system supports blind and
          low-vision users with NPU-based obstacle warning, offline speech,
          and a local LLM agent for closing touch-first app tasks through
          voice. The project made the
          potential of mobile NPUs concrete for me, and it made engineering
          optimization feel like a field with real room for research and
          product judgment.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a
            href="/anvil"
            class="underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent"
          >ANVIL</a> came out of the overlap between those two tracks:
          RAFNet gave me a practical CV foundation, while TongXing made the
          NPU constraints concrete. Standard flow-based VFI breaks down
          under INT8 quantization, so I looked for a graph that fit the
          accelerator instead of forcing the accelerator to imitate a
          desktop model. The result reuses H.264 decoder motion vectors
          instead of learning optical flow. The arXiv preprint is public,
          and I am continuing to reorganize the work into a more systematic
          version. The project page collects the training code, the Android
          demo, and the paper artifacts.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/NihilDigit/waybar-ai-usage"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent"
          >waybar-ai-usage</a>, a Waybar widget that shows quota and reset
          time for Claude Code, Codex CLI, Copilot, and OpenCode Zen, began
          as a small tool for my own desktop. It became my first real open
          source maintenance experience after users started filing issues
          and PRs, including multi-browser support and support for providers
          they used themselves. It's packaged on AUR.
        </p>

        <p>
          I also keep
          <a
            href="https://github.com/NihilDigit/coding-agents-setup"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent"
          >coding-agents-setup</a>, a personal setup repository for coding agents.
          It is where I keep the tools, shell helpers, skills layout, and
          Codex/Claude rule files that I actually use and keep testing
          across my own machines.
        </p>

        <p>
          I also contribute upstream to apps I actually use.
          <a
            href="https://github.com/open-ani/animeko"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent"
          >open-ani/animeko</a> is where I work on cloud download,
          Windows on Arm64 support, HLS playback behavior, and smaller
          UI/data-flow pieces.
          <a
            href="https://github.com/sinelaw/fresh"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent"
          >sinelaw/fresh</a> is where I have been fixing platform
          packaging and editor behavior issues, including Windows ARM64
          release artifacts and vi-mode register handling.
        </p>

        <p>
          A short list of things I'm into: LLMs, Linux, ACGN, and music
          &mdash; rock, folk, and songs that carry history with them.
          Beyond just using them, I find different language models
          genuinely fascinating &mdash; each one has its own character,
          and I spend a lot of hours just talking to them.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/NihilDigit/focuswell"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent"
          >FocusWell</a> is one of the more personal ones: an Android-first
          time accounting app I wrote for my own attention and energy
          patterns. It turns real day-to-day friction into a tool I can
          actually use.
        </p>
      </section>

      <hr class="my-12 border-border" />

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-5 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-muted-foreground">
          Education
        </h2>
        <dl class="grid grid-cols-[6rem_1fr] gap-x-6 gap-y-2 font-mono text-sm">
          <dt class="text-muted-foreground tabular-nums">2023 &ndash;</dt>
          <dd>
            B.S. in Intelligence Science<br />
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">
              College of Science · NCST · Tangshan, Hebei, China
            </span>
          </dd>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <hr class="my-12 border-border" />

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-5 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-muted-foreground">
          Contact
        </h2>
        <dl class="grid grid-cols-[6rem_1fr] gap-x-6 gap-y-2 font-mono text-sm">
          <dt class="text-muted-foreground">Email</dt>
          <dd class="space-y-1">
            <div>
              <a
                href="mailto:spencerliu@stu.ncst.edu.cn"
                class="hover:text-accent"
              >spencerliu<span class="text-muted-foreground">[at]</span>stu.ncst.edu.cn</a>
              <span class="text-muted-foreground"> · school</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <a
                href="mailto:starse.nd233@gmail.com"
                class="hover:text-accent"
              >starse.nd233<span class="text-muted-foreground">[at]</span>gmail.com</a>
              <span class="text-muted-foreground"> · personal</span>
            </div>
          </dd>

          <dt class="text-muted-foreground">GitHub</dt>
          <dd>
            <a
              href="https://github.com/NihilDigit"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
              class="hover:text-accent">@NihilDigit</a
            >
          </dd>

          <dt class="text-muted-foreground">ORCID</dt>
          <dd>
            <a
              href="https://orcid.org/0009-0004-9426-3713"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
              class="hover:text-accent">0009-0004-9426-3713</a
            >
          </dd>

          <dt class="text-muted-foreground">Telegram</dt>
          <dd>
            <a
              href="https://t.me/NihilDigit"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
              class="hover:text-accent">@NihilDigit</a
            >
          </dd>
        </dl>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .cv-peek {
    position: relative;
    width: 7.4rem;
    height: 5.15rem;
    min-width: 44px;
    min-height: 44px;
    overflow: visible;
    perspective: 34rem;
    -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
  }

  .cv-peek__frame {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    width: 7.4rem;
    height: 5.15rem;
    overflow: visible;
    clip-path: inset(-4.8rem -4.8rem 0 -4.8rem);
  }

  .cv-peek__paper {
    position: absolute;
    left: 1.25rem;
    top: 0.72rem;
    display: grid;
    width: 6.15rem;
    min-height: 7.55rem;
    align-content: start;
    gap: 0.34rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.375rem;
    background: var(--background);
    padding: 0.78rem 0.68rem;
    color: var(--foreground);
    box-shadow: 0 0.7rem 1.5rem rgb(0 0 0 / 0.08);
    transform: translate3d(0, 0, 0) rotate(-4deg);
    transition:
      transform 320ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1),
      border-color 180ms ease,
      color 180ms ease,
      box-shadow 320ms cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
  }

  .cv-peek:hover .cv-peek__paper,
  .cv-peek:focus-visible .cv-peek__paper {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    color: var(--accent);
    box-shadow: 0 0.95rem 1.9rem rgb(0 0 0 / 0.12);
    transform: translate3d(-1.2rem, -1.05rem, 0) rotate(-8deg);
  }

  .cv-peek:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px dashed var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 0.35rem;
  }

  .cv-peek__fold {
    position: absolute;
    top: -1px;
    right: -1px;
    width: 1.35rem;
    height: 1.35rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--muted);
    clip-path: polygon(100% 0, 0 0, 100% 100%);
    transition: border-color 180ms ease;
  }

  .cv-peek:hover .cv-peek__fold,
  .cv-peek:focus-visible .cv-peek__fold {
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .cv-peek__label {
    width: fit-content;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    padding: 0.13rem 0.3rem;
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace;
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }

  .cv-peek__title {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.96rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .cv-peek__rule {
    display: block;
    height: 1px;
    width: 100%;
    margin-top: 0.08rem;
    background: var(--border);
  }

  .cv-peek__rule--short {
    width: 62%;
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .cv-peek__paper {
      transition: border-color 180ms ease, color 180ms ease;
    }

    .cv-peek:hover .cv-peek__paper,
    .cv-peek:focus-visible .cv-peek__paper {
      transform: translate3d(0, 0, 0) rotate(-4deg);
    }
  }
</style>
